Self-hosting n8n has no licence fee. You would pay for the machine instead of the €{{ cost.n8n_eur }}. A cloud n8n keeps execution data on n8n's side. The Gmail trigger has already received the raw email by then. If the inbox is sensitive, turn off saving execution data in n8n, or run n8n on your own machine. The placeholder map from the Python runner stays in the file you choose. Do not commit that file on a real job.

## What this does not do

It does not send the reply. It does not file the tax return. It does not decide which client to call. Those are on the shortlist as "don't automate", with the reason next to them.
